      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the advice. i've already controlled for income, but even in similar income brackets, the neighborhoods with higher percentages of certain minority groups seem to have a different profile in the data. sometimes the income variable doesn't fully explain the variance in the theft rates. \n\nfrom an actuarial standpoint, if we see that the ethnic makeup of these ZIP codes is changing rapidly alongside the crime trend, is it considered sound practice to weight those demographic shifts as high-impact risk factors in a predictive model? i want to make sure we aren't missing a key predictive variable.",
